{'symbol': 'JCI', 'date': '2021-12-08 17:01:00', 'title': 'JOHNSON CONTROLS INCREASES QUARTERLY DIVIDEND 26% TO 34 CENTS PER SHARE IN LINE WITH CAPITAL DEPLOYMENT STRATEGY', 'text': 'CORK, IRELAND, DEC. 8, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- JOHNSON CONTROLS (NYSE: JCI), THE GLOBAL LEADER FOR SMART, HEALTHY AND SUSTAINABLE BUILDINGS, TODAY ANNOUNCED AN INCREASE TO ITS REGULAR QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND TO $0.34 PER COMMON SHARE, FROM $0.27 PREVIOUSLY, REPRESENTING AN INCREASE OF 26 PERCENT. THE INCREASE WILL BE EFFECTIVE FROM THE FISCAL FIRST QUARTER DIVIDEND PAYMENT, WHICH WAS APPROVED BY THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS TODAY AND WILL BE PAYABLE ON JANUARY 14, 2022 TO SHAREHOLDERS OF RECORD AT THE CLOSE OF BUSINESS ON DECEMBER 20, 2021.'}